B(2) Email Spam Detection using Binary Classification
1. Aim
To classify emails into two categories (Spam and Not Spam) using K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) and Support Vector Machine (SVM), and compare their performance.
2. Theory
What is binary classification?

Binary classification is a machine learning technique used to classify data into two categories.

In our practical:
Class	Meaning
0	Normal Email (Not Spam)
1	Abnormal Email (Spam)

Example:
- "Hello, how are you?" → Not Spam
- "Congratulations! You won a free prize" → Spam
