6. Performance Comparison
Parameter	KNN	SVM
Full form	K-Nearest Neighbors	Support Vector Machine
Learning type	Supervised	Supervised
Method	Nearest neighbors	Separating boundary
Training	Simple	Finds optimal boundary
Prediction	Can be slower on large datasets	Generally efficient
Main parameter	K value	Kernel

Conclusion: Both algorithms can classify spam emails. SVM often performs well on high-dimensional text data, while KNN is easy to understand and implement. Actual performance depends on the dataset.
7. Viva Questions and Answers
Q1. What is spam detection?

Spam detection is the process of identifying unwanted or fake emails.

Q2. What is binary classification?

Classification into two categories.

Q3. What is KNN?

KNN stands for K-Nearest Neighbors. It classifies data using its nearest neighbors.

Q4. What is SVM?

SVM stands for Support Vector Machine. It separates different classes using a decision boundary.

Q5. What is TF-IDF?

TF-IDF converts text into numerical values based on the importance of words.

Q6. What is training data?

Data used to train a machine learning model.

Q7. What is testing data?

Data used to check model performance.

Q8. What is accuracy?

Accuracy measures how many predictions are correct.

Q9. What is a kernel in SVM?

A kernel helps SVM classify data when the separation is not straightforward.

Q10. Which algorithm is better for spam detection?

SVM often works well for text classification, but the better algorithm depends on the dataset.